# Stable short device name for the spindle VFD's USB-RS485 adapter.
# Install to /etc/udev/rules.d/ on the Milo Pi.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS:
#
# mb2hal cannot open /dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Serial-if00-port0. That
# path is 49 characters and mb2hal uses fixed-size buffers, so it fails at
# startup with:
#     mb2hal get_tx_connection ERR: ... cannot connect to link, ret[-1] fd[-1]
# mbpoll opens the identical path without complaint, which is what isolated
# the fault to mb2hal rather than to permissions, the adapter or the port.
#
# /dev/ttyUSB0 is not safe to hardcode instead: the number depends on what
# else is plugged in and in what order, and a USB SD-card reader has already
# been on this Pi during this build. A config pinned to ttyUSB0 works until
# the day it silently addresses something else.
#
# So: a short, stable symlink. QinHeng CH340 (1a86:7523).
#
# WARNING: this adapter reports NO serial number, so the rule can only match
# on vendor:product. A SECOND CH340 adapter on this Pi would be ambiguous and
# the symlink could attach to the wrong one. If that ever happens, pin it to a
# physical USB port by adding KERNELS=="1-1.2" (or whichever) to the rule.

SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", SYMLINK+="milo-vfd", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
